From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sydney <sydney@hyphen-emdash.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:03:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Move search state out of brain

A search used to change the brain it searched: block usage, the current
block index, the current error and the jiggle all lived on the brain, and
jiggle called the global rand(). Two renderers sharing a brain, as the
left and right renderers do, stepped on each other.

All of that now lives in a search_state that the renderer owns, seeded
with its own std::mt19937. Which sounds are switched on moves there too,
so turning a sound on or off no longer touches the brain. Searching takes
a const brain&, and block::compare takes the other block's usage as an
argument.

The .brain format is unchanged. The fields that used to hold this state
are still written, with their old defaults, and ignored on reading.

search_synapses also stops writing a reduced synapse count back into the
caller's search_params.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
